Sun Nov 22 09:40:57 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.1.0:
  * Design agent with Images, memory, Missions and workspaces.
  * Hardening, Tauri 2.12, Node 24.22.3; opencode >= 2.3.0 minimum.
  * CVE-2026-120222: undici DoS in cache interceptor (boo#1290279)
  * CVE-2026-120415: undici leak via tuple headers (boo#1290311)
  * CVE-2026-120423: undici SRI bypass via whitespace (boo#1290322)
  * CVE-2026-116630: undici leak via revalidation (boo#1290340)
  * CVE-2026-116592: undici poisoning via redirects (boo#1290356)
  * CVE-2026-120474: undici leak via same-origin (boo#1290376)
- Requires nodejs24 >= 24.22 and opencode >= 2.3.0.
- Rebase codenomad-system-node.patch and
  codenomad-no-pwa-assets.patch for the new resources script.
- Drop esbuild-0.21.5.tar.gz and esbuild-0.25.12.tar.gz, add
  esbuild-0.28.2.tar.gz; refresh rollup-4.52.5.tar.gz to
  rollup-4.68.1.tar.gz and both vendor trees (566/195 crates).
- Re-strip node_modules.obscpio (110 tarballs, 162 binaries) and
  regen package-lock.json integrity and node_modules.sums.
- Re-derive License over the shipped trees (366 crates, drop
  BSD-2-Clause) and keep legacy-container true in _service
  (service aborts without it).
- Carry forward r17 reproducible-build fix (delete staged
  .package-lock.json); drop
  codenomad-deterministic-csp-hashes.patch, obsolete at
  tauri-codegen 2.7.4 which already sorts hashes.
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list

